          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Numbers like
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msqrt
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqrt{3}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mn 5
                  %msqrt
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}^5\sqrt{3}
            look tied to the usual integers: indeed they are obtained from an integer number by doing operation of 2nd or 5th root. More generally, we can start with the usual integer numbers and do similar algebraic operations, namely form monic polynomials with such integer coefficients and search for roots in a larger ring, obtaining generalized integers – called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+integers"} algebraic integers
            – as solutions of a monic polynomial equation, which makes sense in an arbitrary commutative ring.
          %p
            If we look for solutions of monic equations within
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            %strong integral elements in a ring
            generalize integers in wide context and form a “ring of integers” within a larger ring. This generalizes the standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            inside the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            to various situations like
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+fields"} number fields
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+field"} local
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-archimedean+fields"} non-archimedean fields
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#general_definition General definition
          %p
            In any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unital+ring"} unital ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            one can identify the ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            with the subring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ n 1_R | n\in\mathbb{Z}\}\subseteq R
            of all multiples
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ±
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ±
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi R
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ±
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi R
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi R
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm 1_R, \pm (1_R+1_R), \pm(1_R+1_R+1_R),\ldots
            of the unit element
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is then a left and right
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            via the multiplication with the corresponding multiple of unit, that is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo .
                    %mi m
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n.m = (n 1_R)\cdot m
          %p
            An
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+integer"} algebraic integer
            in a commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is any element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in R
            which satisfies
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation"} equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(r) = 0
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is a nontrivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial"} polynomial
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            are multiplies of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_R
            and the top degree coefficient is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_R
            (in other words, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/root"} root
            of a monic polynomial in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            with the coefficients in
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
          %p
            It can be checked that the set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+integers"} algebraic integers
            (also said to be integral elements) in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            (also said the
            %em ring of integers of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} 1_R
            as unique solutions for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in R
            of equations
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi R
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi R
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_R \cdot x - n 1_R = 0
          %h3#notation_in_number_theory Notation in number theory
          %p
            The subring of integers in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+number+field"} algebraic number field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            (a
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+extension"} field extension
            of
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi K
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_K \hookrightarrow K
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+field"} local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-archimedean+field"} non-archimedean field
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_F
          %h2#OfANumberField Properties in a number field
          %p
            Alternatively, an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in K
            is an
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+integer"} algebraic integer
            if the subring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[\alpha] \hookrightarrow K
            generated by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            is of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank"} rank
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+integers"} algebraic integers
            themselves form a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo ,
                  %mi β
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha, \beta \in \mathcal{O}_K
            are integral, then both
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo −
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha - \beta
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \beta
            are contained in the image of the induced map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[\alpha] \otimes \mathbb{Z}[\beta] \to K
          %h2#OfANonArchimedeanField Properties in a local non-archimedean field
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+field"} local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-archimedean+field"} non-archimedean field
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_F
            is the subring of elements of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm"} norm
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq 1
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+completion"} formal completion
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+field"} number field
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is the formal completion of the ring of integers of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K = \mathbb{Q}
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
                then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi ℚ
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}} \simeq \mathbb{Z}
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
                of ordinary
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime"} prime
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℚ
                        %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}_p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+completion"} formal completion
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
                at
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+numbers"} p-adic numbers
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℚ
                        %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}_p
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_p
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+integers"} p-adic integers
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gaussian+numbers"} Gaussian numbers
                then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_K
                is the ring of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gaussian+integers"} Gaussian integers
            %li
              %p
                The ring of integers of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclotomic+field"} cyclotomic field
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ζ
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}(\zeta_n)
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi ζ
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[\zeta_n]
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclotomic+integers"} cyclotomic integers
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#general General
          %p
            A ring of integers is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+domain"} Dedekind domain
          %h3#function_field_analogy Function field analogy
          %div
            %p
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+field+analogy"} function field analogy
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+fields"} number fields
                    (“
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+fields"} function fields
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curves"} curves
                    over
                    = succeed "\u201D)" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F1"} F1
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+fields"} function fields
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curves"} curves
                    over
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+fields"} finite fields
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝔽
                            %mi q
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_q
                    (
